"""
A message received from a process mailbox. Each MailboxMessage wraps
a payload value with optional metadata about the sender and message
selector.

MailboxMessages are created automatically by `Process>>send:` and
`Process>>send:with:`. They are received by `Process receive`,
`Process receive:`, `Process tryReceive`, and
`Process receiveMatching:`.

```example
| p <Process> |
p := [Process receive payload] fork.
Process sleep: 10.
p send: 42.
p wait
```

```example
| p <Process> |
p := [Process receive selector] fork.
Process sleep: 10.
p send: #doWork with: 'data'.
p wait
```
"""
MailboxMessage subclass: Object
  instanceVars: sender <Process> selector <Symbol> payload

  """
  The process that sent this message, or `nil` for remote
  or system messages.
  """
  method: sender ^<Process> [
      ^sender
  ]

  """
  The message selector (a Symbol), or `nil` if none was
  specified (raw send).
  """
  method: selector ^<Symbol> [
      ^selector
  ]

  """
  The payload value of the message.
  """
  method: payload [
      ^payload
  ]

  """
  Answer true when the sender used `RemoteProcess>>asyncSend:with:` and is
  awaiting a reply; false for fire-and-forget `cast:with:`/`send:`.

  ```example
  | p <Process> |
  p := [Process receive isRequest] fork.
  Process sleep: 10.
  p send: 42.
  p wait  "=> false"
  ```

  ```test
  | p <Process> |
  p := [Process receive isRequest] fork.
  Process sleep: 10.
  p send: 42.
  p wait >>> false
  ```
  """
  method: isRequest ^<Boolean> [ <primitive> ]

  """
  Answer a request-response message with value, routing it back to the
  requester's Future. Signals if the message was not a request or the
  requester is unreachable. Returns value.

  ```example
  | p <Process> |
  p := [[Process receive reply: 1. false] on: Error do: [:e | e return: true]] fork.
  Process sleep: 10.
  p send: 42.
  p wait  "=> true"
  ```

  ```test
  | p <Process> |
  p := [[Process receive reply: 1. false] on: Error do: [:e | e return: true]] fork.
  Process sleep: 10.
  p send: 42.
  p wait >>> true
  ```
  """
  method: reply: value [ <primitive> ]

  """
  Return a string representation of the message.
  """
  method: printString ^<String> [
      ^'a MailboxMessage(', (selector ifNil: ['(raw)'] ifNotNil: [selector]), ')'
  ]
